# Git Workflow

## Commit Format

Use conventional commits: `type: [scope] description`

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `perf`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`

Examples:
```
feat: [auth] add JWT refresh token rotation
fix: [sync] resolve delta cursor pagination
refactor: [api] extract shared validation logic
```

## Rules

- No AI attribution in commits (no Co-Authored-By AI lines)
- Never force push to main/master
- Always use explicit file names with `git add` (never `git add .` or `git add -A`)
- Create feature branches for non-trivial changes
- Commit often with small, focused commits
- Each commit should compile and pass tests independently
- Write commit messages that explain **why**, not just **what**

## Branch Naming

```
feature/<description>
bugfix/<description>
hotfix/<description>
refactor/<description>
```

## Merge Strategy

- Rebase feature branches before merging
- Squash merge only when commit history is noisy
- Delete branches after merge
